Z||000005||stimpy||04-06-2001||02:03 AM||||As a Devil's advocate, I gotta say that parts of the story sound like they are missing. Did George actually order a couple of hundred bucks of Fiero glassware, or was it sent on speculation that he would sell it on consignment for you.  Not that that should make up for a lack of communication, but like Terry said, there is a toll-free #, I;ve called a few times and never had a problem getting through to George. <P>Now, I must add that I have sat and broke bread with George (and Terry) and they impress me as being decent folks. I hope this works out without going ugly. There is already far too much vendor bashing on the forum.||||reg||5
Z||000006||Alex||04-06-2001||09:35 AM||||Well, I received e-mails from Terry and George this morning and all is well now.<P>It was never my intention to "bash" anyone here (OK, I was a bit frustrated by the lack of communication). I really thought that the business might have gone under and I didn't know how to find out for sure except to ask my west coast friends on this forum. <P>Stimpy (you devil you). The glassware was ordered by the Fiero Shop. I had only just put the first few pieces I had made up for auction when I got the call asking for dozens of all the different pieces. We (Sandra and myself) really burned some midnight oil to get that order to Ricmond under the assurance that payment would be sent immediately (I am normally a cash business (which is what my suppliers expect from me) so I was a little hinky). So you can see that after a long time without any communication, I was convinced that there was a problem.<P>On the up side,I have spoken with George and Terry, and find them to be nice friendly people who are really interested in Fieros first and commerce second (this, in my opinion is a good thing). I won't let this little mix-up deter me from dealing with them (as a supplier or as a customer) in the future. <P>In all fairness to Terry, he did tell me that he had no official responsability for the business. I mentioned him simply because he had been my main contact throughout this transaction.<P>Thanks to everyone (especially George an Terry) who replyed.<BR>Alex<BR>P.S. I comunicated with someone (I'm sorry but I've forgotten who) who said "Fieros are like potato chips, you can't have just one"<BR>He was right. At that time I had one, now I have 3 (and one of them is a GT, Terry, so I WILL be getting to work on the GT glassware)<BR>A<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000007||Bruce||04-06-2001||11:31 AM||||Let's set the record straight: George is really a great guy and diligent businessman. I went there some time ago to have a clutch pedal replaced. He could have done the work, taken my money, and said nothing. But, he was honest enough to point out that the problem was something else and I was on my way. Whenever I've talked to him, he's always been honest and detailed.<BR>Sometimes, s**t happens.||||reg||1
